<mj-text mj-class="h2" padding="0 0 14px">
  <%= I18n.t("mailer.hello", username: @username) %>
</mj-text>

<mj-text>
  <%= I18n.t("mailer.confirm_access.body") %>
</mj-text>

<%#
  Same treatment as the two-factor code: the value has to be read off the screen
  and typed back, so it gets the app's tracked-uppercase label face at display
  size. The tracking is doing real work here - it separates the characters so a
  code cannot be misread - which is why it stays where the webfont is stripped.

  Was an <h1> inside a <center>, which made it the loudest thing in the mail and
  a second competing title under the real one.
%>
<mj-text mj-class="label"
         font-size="30px"
         letter-spacing="8px"
         color="<%= MailerTheme::TEXT %>"
         align="center"
         padding="12px 0 16px">
  <%= @confirmation_code %>
</mj-text>

<mj-text mj-class="footer" padding="0 0 4px">
  <%= I18n.t("mailer.confirm_access.expires") %>
</mj-text>
